# copy to site.env and fill; site.env is never committed. A value set here is the site default. For the override variables
# (ALLREDUCE_IPC ENFORCE_TOOL_CHOICE SPLIT_KV_STATIC SHREW_VARIANT AUX_NO_BUNDLE KV_MIB KV_GIB OFFLOAD_GIB HEALTH_TIMEOUT_S
# RESTART_POLICY EXTRA_SERVE_ARGS MAXSEQ DSPARK REUSE_REL_LOGITS LOCAL_SPLIT_KV GLOBAL_SPLIT_TUNED CONV_TAIL_CACHE MPS AUX_MPS_PCT; list in prod_env.sh) the same variable on the command line wins and prints a `note:` line;
# for every other variable (IMAGE, GPUS, WORKDIR …) the value here wins.
# Image: ONE image for all four services (Inkling, Nemotron, shrew-ocr, embed/rerank) = ink11nemo-r2-minimal (ink11kva + the
# Nemotron files 0071/0089, minus PyNvVideoCodec/PyAV/OpenCV whose bundled ffmpeg had HIGH CVEs: NO video, no mp4/aac audio;
# same library versions, the aux bundles still match). Trivy + Grype: 0 CRITICAL/HIGH. Pinned by digest:
EXPECT_DIGEST=sha256:22d7a0cc2f77f5ce16a04b84bd33931fc7a7f3986a5b77f679969f8feb043ce8   # ink11nemo-r2-minimal (pushed 11-17)
IMAGE=btbtyler09/vllm-cuda@sha256:22d7a0cc2f77f5ce16a04b84bd33931fc7a7f3986a5b77f679969f8feb043ce8   # or <registry>/vllm-cuda@sha256:22d7a0cc...
# (or, digest unset, the local tag btbtyler09/vllm-cuda:0.34.0rc1.dev307-cu130-ink11nemo-r2-minimal: create checks its OVERLAY.txt)
# Rollback to ink11nemo-minimal (video + all audio, but 22 Grype HIGH in OpenCV's ffmpeg):
# EXPECT_DIGEST=sha256:1e567856bfddcd9b36f5f4234e1abe4d35ec3a3a1ba461f9e9f8129d7796c3cf
# IMAGE=<registry>/vllm-cuda@sha256:1e567856bfddcd9b36f5f4234e1abe4d35ec3a3a1ba461f9e9f8129d7796c3cf
# Rollback to ink11kva-minimal (Inkling and aux only; create-nemotron.sh refuses it: no ink11nemo section):
# EXPECT_DIGEST=sha256:1fc652f40b78104991ed576ca5cc882162972ed4705900fbb959cb83158ed509
# IMAGE=<registry>/vllm-cuda@sha256:1fc652f40b78104991ed576ca5cc882162972ed4705900fbb959cb83158ed509
# Rollback to the previous image (ink9.1-minimal):
# EXPECT_DIGEST=sha256:f5740ac43e0b9fd15b588e909d50dfe52e5655684c9fb869cb3ea15006fe1913
# IMAGE=<registry>/vllm-cuda@sha256:f5740ac43e0b9fd15b588e909d50dfe52e5655684c9fb869cb3ea15006fe1913
# (ink8-minimal sha256:db35ec5c120cce8860733997b61451b26fca084e16947957498f8bb5aea9ec74 also needs
#  REUSE_REL_LOGITS=0 LOCAL_SPLIT_KV=0 GLOBAL_SPLIT_TUNED=0: create refuses the new defaults on ink8)
MODEL_DIR=/models/Inkling-2-Small-NVFP4     # or the original Inkling-2-Small dir (rollback / comparison)
WORKDIR=/var/tmp/inkling                    # kernel cache, aux bundles, logs; needs ~20 GB
GPUS=                                       # the TP GPU UUIDs (default TP 8), comma separated (nvidia-smi --query-gpu=uuid --format=csv,noheader);
#                                           # nvidia-smi indices (0,1,2,3) are accepted too and turned into UUIDs
# TP=8                                      # tensor-parallel size = number of cards in GPUS (NGPU is the old name)
NETWORK=                                    # the internal docker network the gateway reaches
AUX_ROOT=/models                            # holds shrew-ocr-preview-v0.5-FP8, nemotron-embed-vl-1b-runtime, nemotron-rerank-vl-1b-runtime
#                                           # (and shrew-ocr-runtime = the previous v0.4 GPTQ dir, kept for rollback)
# SHREW_VARIANT=fp8-v0.5                    # shrew-ocr checkpoint: fp8-v0.5 (default) | gptq-v0.4 (previous line; RUNBOOK "ROLLBACK")
SERVED_NAME=inkling                         # model name the gateway forwards
# start-all.sh: the aux services, started in this order after Inkling. Entries separated by ';', each
#   SERVICE GPU_UUID[,GPU_UUID...] [INSTANCE] [nobundle]   SERVICE = shrew-ocr | embed | rerank; INSTANCE numbers copies (vllm-shrew-ocr-1, -2 …);
#   several UUIDs = one endpoint with that many data-parallel replicas (needs nobundle; RUNBOOK "Shared GPUs and data parallelism");
#   nobundle = start that one without a kernel bundle (a shrew-ocr checkpoint that has no bundle yet)
AUX_SERVICES=""                             # e.g. "shrew-ocr GPU-aaaa 1; shrew-ocr GPU-bbbb 2; rerank GPU-cccc; embed GPU-cccc"
# PUBLISH=127.0.0.1:8000                    # only if the gateway reaches the service through a host port
# EXTRA_SERVE_ARGS="--kv-cache-dtype fp8"   # optional stock vllm serve flags, appended to the serve flags. This one: FP8 KV cache (see RUNBOOK)
#                                           # split on spaces, quotes are NOT honoured: a JSON value must have no space in it
# --- optional, defaults shown ---
# KV_GIB=32                                 # Inkling KV cache per card (RUNBOOK "Memory per card")
# OFFLOAD_GIB=256                           # host RAM for the CPU KV pool, total over the TP ranks, filled at boot
# HEALTH_TIMEOUT_S=3600                     # create-inkling.sh wait (create-aux.sh: 1200). Set here, it replaces the aux 1200 s too
# RESTART_POLICY=no                         # unless-stopped when recreating for keeps
# FIPS_ENABLED_OVERRIDE_FILE=/run/vllm/fips-disabled  # file containing 0; container-only FIPS opt-out; host remains in FIPS mode
#                                           # Set it ONLY on the FIPS host: a kernel without /proc/sys/crypto has no mount point
#                                           # for it and every container fails at docker run (preflight WARNs)
# ALLREDUCE_IPC=0                           # 0 NCCL (default) | tune: ONE boot that tunes the PCIe all-reduce and saves it | tuned:
#                                           # every boot after that, reads the saved tune | 1: image behaviour, hours every boot,
#                                           # do not use (RUNBOOK "All-reduce")
# P2P_DISABLE=0                             # 1: NCCL over host shared memory instead of GPU peer-to-peer DMA (NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=1).
#                                           # Stability A/B for host hangs on boards with PCIe switches; slower. Needs
#                                           # ALLREDUCE_IPC=0. Boot log must show "via SHM" and no "via P2P" (RUNBOOK "P2P")
# ENFORCE_TOOL_CHOICE=1  SPLIT_KV_STATIC=1  # see RUNBOOK "If step 3 fails" / "Cleanup and rollback"
# --- Inkling settings (RUNBOOK "Opt-in: DSpark draft, bias reuse, more sequences" and "ink11"); defaults shown ---
# MAXSEQ=32                                 # --max-num-seqs. 128: up to 128 requests decode together instead of 32 (more
#                                           # throughput above 32 users; ~+0.4 GiB graph memory measured on a 6-layer slice)
# DSPARK=0                                  # 1: speculative decoding with the checkpoint's DSpark draft (mtp.safetensors).
#                                           # Needs the ink9.1 image or later (ink11 included)
# REUSE_REL_LOGITS=1                        # ON since the ink11 kit; 0 turns it off. Attention reuses the relative logits it
#                                           # already computed (ink9+). sm_120 numerics passed 11-15
# LOCAL_SPLIT_KV=1                          # ON since the ink11 kit; 0 turns it off. Split-KV sliding-window decode (ink9.1+)
# GLOBAL_SPLIT_TUNED=1                      # ON since the ink11 kit; 0 turns it off. Global split count from the SM count (ink9.1+)
# CONV_TAIL_CACHE=1                         # ink11 tail-only short-conv state cache (INKLING2_CONV_TAIL_CACHE). 0 = the dense
#                                           # cache of ink10 and before: the ROLLBACK for the KV accounting change
# --- TP4 (ink11 KVA). Uncomment the block, put 4 cards in GPUS ---
# TP=4
# GPUS=GPU-aaaa,GPU-bbbb,GPU-cccc,GPU-dddd  # or GPUS=0,1,2,3 (indices); check the socket in nvidia-smi topo -m
# KV_GIB=10                                 # per card, the MAXIMUM at TP4 on 96 GB cards (12 OOMs at boot).
#                                           # 10 GiB FP8 = 1,852,556 KV tokens = 7.07 x 262,144 at TP4 (measured)
# EXTRA_SERVE_ARGS="--kv-cache-dtype fp8 --enable-prompt-tokens-details"   # FP8 KV; usage reports cached prompt tokens
# DSPARK=0
# REUSE_REL_LOGITS=1  LOCAL_SPLIT_KV=1  GLOBAL_SPLIT_TUNED=1  CONV_TAIL_CACHE=1   # the defaults, written out
# OFFLOAD_GIB=256                           # total over the 4 ranks (unchanged meaning)
# ALLREDUCE_IPC=tune                        # FIRST boot only (~2 min extra), then ALLREDUCE_IPC=tuned for every boot after
#                                           # (RUNBOOK "All-reduce"). TP4, same ink11 build: c1 80 -> 102 tok/s
#                                           # (+27%), c4 240 -> 274 (+14%), c8 385 -> 425 (+10%), same at 32k. The tune is per
#                                           # box and GPU order: run the tune boot on the serving box itself.
#                                           # Full suite tuned: 2k c1 97.4 tok/s (TPOT 9.75 ms, NCCL 12.45), c32 838,
#                                           # 64k c4 111; 10-min soak 16 x 64k distinct: 553 tok/s, 0 preemptions,
#                                           # 0 server errors, text/json PASS under load. A boot that is not really tuned
#                                           # makes create-inkling.sh print ERROR and exit 1 (container left running)
# MPS=0                                     # 1: all GPU services run under ONE host MPS daemon (./mps.sh start, root): aux services
#                                           # capped at AUX_MPS_PCT % of the SMs, Inkling uncapped. UNTESTED on real docker; proven
#                                           # only via the pod-side shim. RUNBOOK "MPS" (enable, rollback, server-failure recovery)
# AUX_MPS_PCT=                              # required with MPS=1, 1..100. NO default: set it from the interference measurement
# PORT=8000
# AUX_BUNDLES=$WORKDIR/aux-bundles          # where bundle-<svc>/ were extracted
# AUX_NO_BUNDLE=1                           # aux services without a kernel bundle
# KV_MIB=                                   # aux KV cache in MiB; applies to EVERY aux service: better on the command line
# AUX_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.15 # startup reservation per auxiliary GPU; validate alongside Inkling
#
# --- Nemotron 3.5 Super VL (create-nemotron.sh) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEMOTRON_GPUS=4,5                         # 2 cards not used by Inkling (UUIDs or indices; must not be in GPUS)
# NEMOTRON_DIR=/path/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-runtime   # the runtime model dir (config.json sha256 35189a80...)
#                                           # (Nemotron runs on IMAGE above; start-all.sh starts it after Inkling when NEMOTRON_GPUS is set)
# NEMOTRON_BUNDLE=$WORKDIR/nemotron-bundles/bundle-nemotron     # extracted bundle-nemotron.tar.gz (default path)
# NEMOTRON_SPEC=mtp3                        # default (MTP-3); none needs NEMOTRON_NO_BUNDLE=1 (the bundle is mtp3's)
# NEMOTRON_OFFLOAD_GIB=64                   # pinned host RAM for its CPU KV pool, total over both ranks (32 GiB/rank); 0 = off
# NEMOTRON_PORT=8000  NEMOTRON_PUBLISH=     # container port; host port to publish (default none)
